2026-11-06T03:02:14.4640238Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4652438Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4653234Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4653702Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4653929Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4654134Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4654509Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4654818Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4655262Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4655498Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4655614Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4655900Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4656176Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4656481Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4657056Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:02:14.4657293Z 
